# Restoration Magic's mana value is its mana cost's, {W} = 1, whichever mode is chosen (CR 702.183a, 202.3). Curaga costs
# {W}{3}{W} to cast, so counting the mode's cost would make it mana value 5. Bot2's Disdainful Stroke ("Counter target
# spell with mana value 4 or greater") is the test. Positive control, turn 2: Bot2's own Serra Paragon (mana value 4) is
# a legal target and is countered. Turn 4: with only Bot2's Pyroclasm (mana value 2) and Bot1's Curaga on the stack the
# Stroke has no legal target and is not offered (the refusal), so Curaga resolves and Bot1 gains 6 life.

